            <ArticleTitle>[Interrelations between subjective and personal characteristics of patients with hypertension and the indicators of central and cerebral hemodynamics].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study was made of the correlation between subjective sensations (headache), the degree of disorder of cerebral hemodynamics and personal peculiarities in 101 patients with hypertensive disease. A high degree (100%) of neurotization, a decrease in the level of the cerebral blood flow in the presence of acutely raised tension of the cerebral small vessels and disorders of the venous outflow were revealed. An insignificant elevation of tension of the cerebral small vessels with the preserved arterial blood flow and normal venous outflow was detected in the patients who did not suffer from headaches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
